<title>GERMANY: Opel -96 profits likely at high end of range.</title>
<headline>Opel -96 profits likely at high end of range.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adam Opel AG management board chairman David Herman said on Thursday that he expected 1996 profits to be at the high end of a previously-cited range of 300-350 million marks ($180-210 million).</p>
<p>&quot;It would surprise me if we did not come in at the upper end of the range. I have good reasons to say that,&quot; Herman told a news conference.</p>
<p>The German unit of General Motors Corp in 1995 reported 1995 profits of 363 million marks. ($ = 1.653 German Marks)</p>
</text>
